;; Make the detached PR-monitor survive a one-shot workflow process exit.
;; Followup from #1183: the observe phase now starts the PR-monitor on a
;; detached future and returns :observe/status :monitoring so the SDLC reaches
;; :done. But in a one-shot `bb miniforge run`, the JVM exits at :done and the
;; future dies — so the autonomous comment -> fix -> resolve loop never runs to
;; completion in a dogfood. This spec closes that gap.

{:spec/title "Persist and resume the PR-monitor so it survives a one-shot CLI exit"
 :version "1.0.0"
 :type :feature
 :priority :high

 :spec/description
 "After #1183, the observe phase detaches the PR-monitor onto an in-process
  future. That is correct for a long-lived deployment, but in a one-shot
  `bb miniforge run` the process exits when the workflow reaches :done, killing
  the monitor before it can respond to any PR review comments. The autonomous
  comment -> fix -> resolve capability therefore never actually exercises in a
  dogfood run.

  Close the gap so PR monitoring outlives the workflow process:

  1. On entry, the observe phase persists the monitor's work-list (the open PRs
     it would monitor, the self-author, and the poll/budget config) to a
     durable location under a gitignored runtime path.

  2. A resumable entry point — a `miniforge monitor` CLI command (or equivalent)
     — reads that persisted work-list and runs the same run-pr-monitor-loop
     out-of-band, so monitoring can continue (or be re-attached) after the
     one-shot workflow process has exited.

  3. The persisted work-list is keyed so a later `miniforge monitor` invocation
     resumes the right PRs idempotently, and a PR that has since merged/closed
     is dropped from the work-list rather than polled forever.

  This is the prerequisite for the autonomous comment -> fix -> resolve loop
  (work/pr-comment-monitoring.spec.edn) to actually complete in a dogfood: the
  monitor must be able to run to a terminal condition outside the workflow
  process that opened the PR."

 :spec/intent
 {:type :feature
  :scope ["components/workflow/src/ai/miniforge/workflow/observe_phase.clj"
          "components/pr-lifecycle/src/ai/miniforge/pr_lifecycle/monitor_loop.clj"
          "components/pr-lifecycle (monitor work-list persistence + resume)"
          "the CLI base (a `miniforge monitor` resumable command)"]}

 :current-state
 {:detach "observe starts the monitor on an in-process future and exposes it at :execution/pr-monitor-future (#1183)"
  :gap "a one-shot `bb miniforge run` exits the JVM at :done, killing the future; no persisted work-list and no out-of-band entry point exist, so monitoring never resumes"}

 :target-state
 {:persist "observe writes the monitor work-list (open PRs + self-author + poll/budget config) to a gitignored runtime path"
  :resume "a `miniforge monitor` command reads the work-list and runs run-pr-monitor-loop out-of-band"
  :idempotent "resuming re-attaches the correct PRs; merged/closed PRs are pruned from the work-list, not polled forever"
  :dogfood "after a one-shot run completes, invoking the resume path lets the comment -> fix -> resolve loop run to a terminal condition"}

 :spec/constraints
 ["Runtime state (the persisted work-list) must live under a gitignored path — never git-tracked, never under the worktree root"
  "Reuse run-pr-monitor-loop and the existing monitor config shape; do not fork a second monitor implementation"
  "Persisting on observe entry must not re-introduce a blocking call on the workflow thread (keep observe non-blocking, per #1183)"
  "The resume command must be safe to run when the work-list is empty or all PRs are already merged (no-op, clear exit)"
  "Return anomalies as data at component boundaries; the resume command surfaces a clear status rather than throwing"]

 :testing-strategy
 {:unit-tests
  ["observe entry writes a work-list containing the open PRs, self-author, and poll/budget config to the configured runtime path"
   "the resume entry point reads a persisted work-list and starts run-pr-monitor-loop for those PRs"
   "resume with an empty / all-merged work-list is a clean no-op"
   "a merged/closed PR is pruned from the work-list on the next resume rather than polled"]}

 :spec/acceptance-criteria
 [{:criterion "observe persists a resumable monitor work-list"
   :verification "After enter-observe, the configured gitignored runtime path contains the open-PR work-list + config"}
  {:criterion "the monitor resumes out-of-band"
   :verification "Invoking the resume entry point against the persisted work-list runs the monitor loop for those PRs without the original workflow process"}
  {:criterion "resume is idempotent and prunes terminal PRs"
   :verification "A merged PR is removed from the work-list on resume; resuming twice does not double-monitor"}
  {:criterion "empty work-list is a safe no-op"
   :verification "Resume with no open PRs exits cleanly with a status, no exception"}]

 :estimated-effort "1-2 days"
 :workflow/type :canonical-sdlc}
